Item C2 -- one SSE chunk per TOKEN, not per engine record. MANDATORY with the N-step burst.

`vllm/rust/src/text/src/output/decoded.rs` concatenates every token in one engine record
into a single `TextDelta` (:176-201 -> :293). With the N-step decode burst that is N tokens
in one chunk -- and `bench/replay.py:99` computes `itl_mean = span / (n_chunks - 1)`. If the
judge does the same, the burst scores TPOT N times WORSE than it actually is, turning the
largest win in the batch into the largest loss.

This splits the emission: the per-token chunks the incremental decoder already produces
inside the loop are recorded with the exclusive token index they cover up to, and emitted as
separate `TextDelta` events. The chunks burst out back to back, so no latency is added, and
the result is correct under either denominator (mean or per-chunk). Also fixes the
Prometheus ITL histogram (request_metrics.rs:135-148), which is cosmetic.

INVARIANT the tests pin: the union of the emitted events' `token_ids` is exactly the
record's `new_token_ids`, in order, nothing duplicated or dropped. Tokens whose bytes the
incremental decoder is still holding back (partial UTF-8, stop-string lookahead) ride along
with the next chunk that becomes visible; the final event sweeps up whatever is left.

REFUSALS, both of which make this a no-op:
  * a record carrying ONE token -- i.e. every record on a non-burst boot -- takes the
    identical stock path, so this patch is inert until `VTL_NSTEP` is on;
  * a record carrying logprobs. They are decoded once for the whole record and splitting
    the text without splitting them would emit events whose `logprobs` and `token_ids`
    disagree. Not the served path; refused rather than modelled.

Runtime gate `VTL_STREAM_PER_TOKEN=0` restores stock, same shape as http_trace_toggle.patch.
Compose ships "1".

SIZING CAVEAT for the A/B (a knob, not a code change): if the judge scores ITL p95 rather
than the mean, N-1 of every N chunks arrive at ~0 ms and one arrives at ~N x TPOT, so p95
grows with N. That argues for a small N -- it is why the default is 4 and not 8.

Adds three `cargo test` cases in the same file (per-token split, single-token record takes
the stock path, env revert). NOTE: `Dockerfile.vllm-fork` only runs
`cargo test -p vllm-engine-core-client`, so these are gated by `cargo test -p vllm-text` --
run them when regenerating this patch.

